;; FH-REACT-006 — `v/defhost` is the SOLE inward React host door.
;;
;; The row this fixture proves is about a SURFACE, not a render. Before the
;; door landed, vector-head classification already had three legal answers
;; and one of them was "a declared host descriptor" — the diagnostic that
;; refuses a bad head says so in its own message — while NO public verb
;; produced one. An adopter could read what a host boundary was and could
;; not build one.
;;
;; So the law has two halves and both need proving. `v/defhost` mints the
;; head (`:mints`), and NOTHING ELSE does (`:absent` plus `:pre-door-value`).
;; The absent names are D022's rejected alternatives, spelled here rather
;; than described: each would be the same crossing under a second spelling,
;; with a second set of laws to keep in step.
{:fh/id "FH-REACT-006"
 :fh/law
 "v/defhost is the sole public verb that mints Freehand's third legal vector head: a declaration produces one stable, qualified, NON-CALLABLE host descriptor that classifies as :host, a direct call on it raises :rf.error/view-called-directly rather than answering nil, the pre-door marked map is an ordinary map and an error head, and no other name on the door mints or names a host boundary."

 ;; The head the declaration mints, and how it classifies.
 :mints
 {:head        :fixture/declared-host
  :classifies  :host
  :predicate   true
  :direct-call {:error-id :rf.error/view-called-directly}}

 ;; The value the pilot used to reach PAST the door with, while the door had
 ;; nothing behind it. Nominality is what makes it an ordinary map now.
 :pre-door-value
 {:value {:re-frame.freehand/host true :component "AcmeChart"}
  :predicate false
  :classifies :error
  :error-id   :rf.error/view-bad-head}

 ;; Names that MUST NOT appear on the public door. Each is rejected by name
 ;; in D022 §Alternatives considered.
 :absent ["host" "react-el" "->element"]

 ;; The one name that MUST appear. Stated positively so a rename of the verb
 ;; reds this row rather than passing vacuously through the absence list.
 :present ["defhost"]

 ;; Every declaration states these; there is no default for either, because
 ;; a default would be the substrate choosing a server behaviour silently.
 :required-options [:children :ssr]
 :closed-options   [:callbacks :children :ssr :map-props :props]
 :declaration-error-id :rf.ui.compile/bad-defhost}
